{"t": 1792308664.9335275, "kind": "prompt", "asker": "claude-1", "text": "claude-1 asks: The mall now works but is chest-fed by hand: input chests at (-14.5,-18.5) copper, (-14.5,-14.5) iron, (-7.5,-21.5) wood, claude-2's cells at x -27..-20 y -21..-14, claude-3's gear->belt chain fed from chests (-19.5,-27.5),(-15.5,-27.5) via inserters off the belt at y=-25.5 (runs west from x=21.5 to -21.5, currently empty). Smelting is ~100 tiles away near (74,26) and claude-4/5 near (22,67)-(27,102); base makes ~206 iron plates/min. What is the simplest buildable plan to get iron and copper plates onto the y=-25.5 belt (one lane each) so the mall and depot fill automatically? Give the route, belt counts, and post it as board tasks for claude-4/claude-5 if appropriate.\n[roadmap]\n[>] 0. Mall: belts, inserters, gears, poles, assemblers auto-made into provider chests\n[ ] 1. Plate belt (y=-25.5) delivers iron+copper to mall instead of hand-filled chests\n[ ] 2. Red science 0.5/s sustained into labs\n[ ] 3. Green science automated 0.5/s\n[ ] 4. Steel 0.5/s\n[ ] 5. Mall adds drills, furnaces, circuits\n[board]\n#2 [claimed @claude-2] Mall: inserters + assembling machines -- Zone x -28..-17, y -21..-14 (open ground south of the plate belt). Build 2 assemblers: inserter recipe and assembling-machine-1 recipe, each: input chest -> inserter -> asm -> inserter -> output chest. Fill input chests from depot (iron -13.5,-29.5, gears -8.5,-29.5, circuits -7.5,-29.5). Mark outputs provider 'MALL: inserters' / 'MALL: assemblers'. Power from pole near -23,-22.\n    last note: claude-2: building at x -27..-20, y -21..-14; mall belt feed chest at -7.5,-23.5 also loading iron\n[crew] claude-1, claude-2, claude-3"}
