{"t": 1792308677.9911523, "kind": "result", "name": "designs", "out": "Proven designs (validated in game). Stamp one with `stamp`, then build it with build_ghosts.\n- gear-circuit-block (14x7): Gears and electronic circuits from one plate belt: a gear assembler (1 gear/s, fed by 3 inserters), a copper-cable assembler direct-inserting into a circuit assembler (one cable assembler limits circuits to 0.67/s). Output belt: gears on one lane, circuits on the other. Uses 2.67 iron + 1 copper plates/s. Power about 0.3 MW (3 assemblers + 11 inserters).\n    in: iron plates + copper plates on separate lanes: belt enters from the west at tile (0,0)\n    out: gears 1/s (south lane) + electronic circuits 0.67/s (north lane): belt leaves to the east at tile (13,6)\n    build: assembling-machine-1 3, inserter 12, small-electric-pole 5, transport-belt 30\n- green-science-6 (23x13): Logistic science from plates, gears and circuits: 1 inserter assembler + 1 transport-belt assembler (asm1, ratio 6 green : 1 inserter : 1 belt; the intermediates run at 50% and 25%) put inserters and belts on separate lanes of a belt feeding 6 green-science assemblers (6 s at speed 0.5 = 1/12 per s each): 0.5 green packs/s (30/min). Consumes 0.75 iron plates/s, 0.75 gears/s, 0.5 circuits/s. Power about 0.75 MW (8 assemblers + 17 inserters).\n    in: iron plates + iron gear wheels on separate lanes: belt enters from the south at tile (0,12); electronic circuits (any lane): belt enters from the west at tile (0,0)\n    out: logistic science packs 0.5/s: belt leaves to the east at tile (22,12)\n    build: assembling-machine-1 8, inserter 18, small-electric-pole 8, transport-belt 53\n- lab-row-6 (25x3): 6 labs in a row, fed at the west end from a belt with red + green packs; pairs of inserters pass packs from lab to lab. Full speed for research of 15 s/unit or slower: 0.4 units/s at 15 s (uses 0.4 red + 0.4 green/s), 0.2 units/s at 30 s. Power about 0.55 MW (6 labs x 60 kW + 12 inserters).\n    in: red + green science packs on separate lanes: belt enters from the north at tile (0,0)\n    out: research progress (0.4 units/s at 15 s/unit)\n    build: inserter 12, lab 6, small-electric-pole 6, transport-belt 3\n- red-science-5 (15x7): 5 assembling-machine-1 making automation science packs (5 s recipe at speed 0.5 = 0.1/s each): 0.5 red packs/s (30/min) from 0.5 copper plates/s + 0.5 iron gears/s. Power about 0.45 MW (5 x 77.5 kW + 10 inserters).\n    in: copper plates + iron gear wheels on separate lanes: belt enters from the west at tile (0,0)\n    out: automation science packs 0.5/s: belt leaves to the east at tile (14,6)\n    build: assembling-machine-1 5, inserter 10, small-electric-pole 6, transport-belt 30\n- smelting-column-12 (11x14): 12 stone furnaces (2 rows of 6) on one center input belt carrying ore on one lane and coal on the other (each input inserter feeds its furnace both); plates leave on two outer belts that merge at the top into one output. 3.75 plates/s (225/min) of iron or copper (stone bricks: 1.9/s). Burns 0.27 coal/s. Power: 24 inserters, about 0.1 MW (peak 0.35 MW).\n    in: ore (3.75/s) + coal (0.27/s) on separate lanes of one belt: belt enters from the south at tile (5,13)\n    out: plates 3.75/s (both lanes): belt leaves to the north at tile (10,0)\n    build: inserter 24, small-electric-pole 9, stone-furnace 12, transport-belt 47\n- steam-power-1-2 (12x6): Offshore pump + 1 boiler + 2 steam engines: up to 1.8 MW. Burns up to 0.45 coal/s at full load (a burner inserter feeds the boiler from the coal input tile: end a coal belt there or put a chest of coal there).\n    in: coal: end a coal belt on, or put a chest of coal at, this tile [tile (0,6)]\n    out: electricity up to 1.8 MW: wire your poles to the small pole on this tile [tile (6,1)]\n    placement: must sit on a shore: stamp it with anchor='offshore-pump' at an offshore_pump_spots entry from find name=water, rotation=<that spot's direction> (the pump faces the water). The rest needs 12x